  "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-9x+36}{(x-3)(x-6)}=-\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-6)},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$",
  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-9x+36}{(x-3)(x-6)}=-\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-6)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(x-6)$ gives\n\n$$\n-9x+36=-3(x-6)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=6$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(6)+36 & =-3(6-6)+B(6-3) \\\\ -18 & =3B \\\\ B & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
